## The idea

Every key has a fixed **rank**; when the cache is full we evict the **lowest** rank. A **SortedSet of ranks** gives the lowest in O(log n), and two dictionaries map key → (value, rank) and rank → key. One design decision must be stated: if a newcomer ranks **below** everything already cached, we still return its value but do **not** cache it — evicting something better to store something worse would be wrong.

## Step by step

1. Get(key): if cached → count a hit and return the value.
2. Otherwise count a miss, fetch the value and rank from the slow source.
3. If the cache is full: look at the lowest cached rank. If the newcomer's rank is lower → count it as rejected and just return the value. Otherwise evict the lowest-ranked entry.
4. Store the newcomer in both dictionaries and the sorted set; return the value.

## Worked example

**Input:** capacity 3; ranks a=10, b=20, c=30, d=5, e=40; Get a, b, c, a, e, d

| Step | What happens |
|---|---|
| Get a, b, c | 3 misses; cache {a10, b20, c30} |
| Get a | hit |
| Get e (40) | miss; full; lowest is a (10) < 40 → evict a → cache {b, c, e} |
| Get d (5) | miss; full; lowest is b (20) but 5 < 20 → do not cache d (rejected); return its value |

**Result:** cache {b, c, e}; d was served but not admitted

## Cost

Get: O(1) for a hit, O(log n) plus one source call for a miss. Memory O(capacity).

## The code (C#, compiled and tested against every part of the question)

```csharp
// IRankedDataSource<TKey,TValue> is provided (Models.cs): Get(key) is slow, GetRank(key) is fixed and distinct.
public class RankCache<TKey, TValue> {
    private readonly int _capacity;
    private readonly IRankedDataSource<TKey, TValue> _source;
    private readonly Dictionary<TKey, TValue> _values = new Dictionary<TKey, TValue>();
    private readonly Dictionary<TKey, int> _rankOf = new Dictionary<TKey, int>();
    private readonly Dictionary<int, TKey> _keyOfRank = new Dictionary<int, TKey>();
    private readonly SortedSet<int> _ranks = new SortedSet<int>();   // .Min = the next to evict

    public long Hits { get; private set; }
    public long Misses { get; private set; }
    public long Rejected { get; private set; }   // served, but not admitted into the cache

    public RankCache(int capacity, IRankedDataSource<TKey, TValue> source) {
        if (capacity <= 0) throw new ArgumentOutOfRangeException(nameof(capacity));
        if (source == null) throw new ArgumentNullException(nameof(source));
        _capacity = capacity;
        _source = source;
    }

    public TValue Get(TKey key) {
        TValue cached;
        if (_values.TryGetValue(key, out cached)) {
            Hits++;
            return cached;
        }

        Misses++;
        TValue value = _source.Get(key);       // the slow call the cache exists to avoid
        int rank = _source.GetRank(key);

        if (_values.Count == _capacity) {
            int lowest = _ranks.Min;
            if (rank < lowest) {
                Rejected++;                     // worth less than everything we hold: do not cache
                return value;
            }
            TKey victim = _keyOfRank[lowest];   // evict the lowest rank
            _ranks.Remove(lowest);
            _keyOfRank.Remove(lowest);
            _values.Remove(victim);
            _rankOf.Remove(victim);
        }

        _values[key] = value;
        _rankOf[key] = rank;
        _keyOfRank[rank] = key;
        _ranks.Add(rank);
        return value;
    }

    public bool Contains(TKey key) {
        return _values.ContainsKey(key);
    }

    public int Count {
        get { return _values.Count; }
    }
}
```

